WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.600
3 minutes to prepare.

2
00:00:01.600 --> 00:00:03.250
3 minutes to speak.

3
00:00:03.250 --> 00:00:05.110
Just your notes in front of you.

4
00:00:05.110 --> 00:00:07.860
Picture a model talk on Senegal.

5
00:00:07.860 --> 00:00:10.160
It features a rice-and-fish dish:

6
00:00:10.160 --> 00:00:11.330
«le ceebu jën».

7
00:00:11.330 --> 00:00:14.710
Behind those three minutes
are months of research.

8
00:00:14.710 --> 00:00:17.020
So how do you turn months of research into

9
00:00:17.020 --> 00:00:19.920
one short talk that holds together?

10
00:00:19.920 --> 00:00:22.990
In this mission, you'll
build a five-part skeleton,

11
00:00:22.990 --> 00:00:26.450
held together by signposts
like «Autrement dit».

12
00:00:26.450 --> 00:00:28.610
Then you'll put a whole talk in order,

13
00:00:28.610 --> 00:00:30.150
chip by chip.

14
00:00:30.150 --> 00:00:33.450
Your mission: work out how
to turn months of research

15
00:00:33.450 --> 00:00:35.240
into three minutes that work.
